\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1 God of my life, through all my days 
\par My grateful powers shall sound Thy praise;
\par My song shall wake with opening light, 
\par And cheer the dark and silent night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 When anxious cares would break my rest,
\par And griefs would tear my throbbing breast, 
\par Thy tuneful praises, raised on high,
\par Shall check the murmur and the sigh.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 When death o'er nature shall prevail, 
\par And all the powers of language fail, 
\par Joy through my swimming eyes shall break,
\par And mean the thanks I cannot speak.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4 But O when that last conflict's o'er,
\par And I am chained to earth no more, 
\par with what glad accents shall I rise 
\par To join the music of the skies!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5 Soon shall I learn the exalted strains 
\par Which echo through the heacenly plains;
\par And emulate, with joy unknown, 
\par The glowing seraphs round the throne. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6 The cheerful tribute will I give 
\par Lon as a deathless soul shall live;
\par A work so sweet, a theme so high, 
\par Demands and crowns eternity.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

